---
import DemoShell from '../DemoShell.astro';
import Control from './Control.astro';
---

<DemoShell
  id="demo-discharge"
  code="D6"
  title="Galvanostatic discharge"
  poster="d6-discharge.svg"
  alt="Cell voltage falling from about 4.2 volts to the 2.5 volt cut-off against discharged capacity, with the open-circuit curve above it"
  aspect="16/10"
  caption="Constant-current discharge of an NMC811 | graphite cell from a single-particle model. The gap between the dashed open-circuit curve and the terminal voltage is the overpotential the current costs. Use hold to compare C-rates."
  presets={[
    { label: 'Fast discharge: 3C loses capacity', state: { 'd6-crate': 3 } },
    { label: 'Big particles: diffusion-limited at 2C', state: { 'd6-radius': 12, 'd6-crate': 2 } },
    { label: 'Cold cell: 0 °C', state: { 'd6-T': 273 } },
  ]}
>
  <fieldset class="panel" slot="panel" disabled>
    <legend>cell · galvanostat</legend>
    <Control id="d6-crate" label="C-rate / h⁻¹" min={0.1} max={4} value={1} step={0.1} />
    <Control id="d6-radius" label="particle R / µm" min={2} max={12} value={6} step={1} />
    <Control id="d6-r0" label="series R₀ / mΩ" min={0} max={60} value={25} step={1} />
    <Control id="d6-T" label="T / K" min={273} max={333} value={298} step={1} />
    <div class="switch-row">
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="d6-ocv" checked /> open-circuit overlay</label>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-readouts">
      <span>capacity <output id="d6-cap">—</output></span>
      <span>mean V <output id="d6-vmean">—</output></span>
      <span>energy <output id="d6-energy">—</output></span>
      <span>ends on <output id="d6-cutoff">—</output></span>
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <p>
      A single-particle model: solid diffusion inside one representative particle per electrode by
      implicit Euler, symmetric Butler–Volmer kinetics inverted analytically, and the two
      open-circuit potential curves.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        It is a single-particle reduction, not a porous-electrode (P2D) model. It carries no
        electrolyte gradient, so above roughly 2C it is optimistic.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open-circuit potential fits follow Chen et al. (2020) for an LG M50 cell. The remaining
        parameters are representative of that format, not a validated reproduction of a measured
        cell.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</DemoShell>

<script>
  import { initWhenVisible } from './runtime';
  initWhenVisible('demo-discharge', async (shell) => {
    const { init } = await import('./d6-discharge');
    init(shell);
  });
</script>
